No.  Skill isn't subjective.

Extinctionism is just as "easy" as a normal ascension: assemble AK, farm for 
200k turns, ascend.  There is the possibility of boredom-induced YASD, but 
that does not make this "conduct" challenging.  Ascending in 15k turns is 
*much* harder than ascending in 40k, or 85k.  

I do realize I'm not completely impartial here; it is certainly possible 
that I'm overestimating exactly how challenging a speed ascension is 
relative to other conducts, or relative to simply ignoring the turn counter.  

> > I read Richard's question differently; speed ascension is skillful but
> > playing valkyries ist not, and playing tourists is skillful but doing
> > an extinctionist is not.

Giving the "bad" classes a score bonus (multiplier, probably) is reasonable, 
but one must be careful not to make the bonus large enough that those 
classes suddenly become the "good" ones, because it is now easier to get 
high scores with them.  

Or the tournament could ignore those differences, but have plenty of role-
based awards.  So, for instance, there would be a "most conducts" ranking 
for each of the 13 classes, and the overall "most conducts" would probably 
go to a Monk or one of the other good classes.  I don't see anything wrong 
with that; ascend a Tourist to try for "Most Conducts - Tourist", then go 
ascend a monk for "Most Conducts - Overall".



